<BaseLayout title="\u201cI\u2019ve paid\u201d meets a payment record." description="Verify the transaction, match the order and prepare a receipt with your business name on it.">
<PageHero eyebrow="The Kora product plan" title="\u201cI\u2019ve paid\u201d meets a payment record." lede="Verify the transaction, match the order and prepare a receipt with your business name on it." />
<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 prose-kora">
<h2>Confirmation comes from the provider</h2>
<p>The planned Paystack integration uses authenticated webhook events and server-side transaction verification. Expected amount, currency, order reference and receiving merchant must match before an order is marked paid.</p>
<h2>A screenshot is a clue</h2>
<p>A customer’s screenshot or forwarded alert may help identify a payment. It does not prove money arrived. Unmatched, partial or overpaid transactions need a review workflow.</p>
<h2>Your order supplies the shopping list</h2>
<p>Item names, quantities and agreed prices come from the saved order. Payment data supplies the amount received and transaction reference. Together they produce a merchant-issued branded PDF receipt.</p>
<h2>Honest status, clear exceptions</h2>
<p>Cash sales are recorded as declared by staff, with an audit trail. They are not labelled provider-verified. Refunds, reversals and late payments require explicit handling. No live bank or payment account is connected to this preview.</p>
<p><a href="/pilot" class="btn btn-primary">Explore the founding pilot</a></p>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
